 some  property inherent to that phylum but a  product of an evolutionary path that  started after the Stentor family began  to branch away of very  very long time ago now Ellucian is weird  and messy it is a knot that sometimes  seems to become more tangled the more we  try to unravel it and stent errs well  their confirmation that no matter how  simple something may seem whether it's  their own surprisingly complex  single-celled bodies or the supposed  universality of the genetic code it only  takes a few what's wise and house to  find yourself and meshed and a web of  questions that is not unlike the  marvelous mysteries first uncovered by  the original microbe hunters hundreds of  years ago their discoveries or  world-changing but so are ours we live  in a time of great knowing of great  uncovering but that has also helped us  realize how many mysteries we have yet  to solve thank you for coming on this  journey with us as we explore the unseen  world that surrounds us if you would  like to get a pin celebrating the  majesty of this peculiar organism we  have Stentor karolius pins available now  there's a link in the description and  also thank you so much to all of our  patrons on patreon who allow us to  continue these explorations and keep our  eyes out for more bizarre happenings in  our microscopes without people like this  the work we're doing here on journey to  the micro cosmos would not be possible  so if you're able to potentially join  them that would be amazing and thank you  to all of the people on this list if you  want to see more from our master of  microscopes James you can check out Jam  and germs on Instagram and if you want  to see more from us here at journey to  the micro cosmos you can find us at  youtube.com slash micro cosmos  you  [Music]

